# Copy to .env and fill in; `make` loads it and passes the values to the engine and the app.
# Hugging Face token (https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens): needed for gated models
# and gives faster downloads. Accept each gated model's license on its Hugging Face page with the
# same account; a fine-grained token also needs "Read access to ... public gated repos".
HF_TOKEN=
# Website crawling: proxy (http://user:pass@host:port or socks5://host:port), a browser to use
# over CDP, and defaults for crawls. All but the proxy are defaults: the app's Settings >
# Crawler saves its own values in the engine, which win.
# TINYLM_PROXY=socks5://127.0.0.1:1080
# TINYLM_CDP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9222
# TINYLM_CRAWL_PER_MINUTE=20
# false: robots.txt is not read (only for sites you may crawl anyway)
# TINYLM_CRAWL_RESPECT_ROBOTS=true
# TINYLM_CRAWL_MAX_PAGES=50
# TINYLM_CRAWL_MAX_DEPTH=2
# true: load pages in the browser at TINYLM_CDP_URL by default (make chrome starts one)
# TINYLM_CRAWL_USE_BROWSER=false
# Links no crawl follows: a part of the address, or a pattern with * for the whole address
# TINYLM_CRAWL_EXCLUDE=["/tag/", "?sort=", "*/forum/*"]
# Web search for finding sites and trailers: a local SearXNG (`make searxng`, free, no key),
# or brave, tavily, exa, perplexity or serper with their API keys. These are defaults: the app's
# Settings > Search saves its own choice in the engine, which wins.
# TINYLM_SEARCH_PROVIDER=searxng
# TINYLM_SEARXNG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8888
# TINYLM_BRAVE_API_KEY=
# TINYLM_TAVILY_API_KEY=
# TINYLM_EXA_API_KEY=
# TINYLM_PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=
# TINYLM_SERPER_API_KEY=
# Only / never these sites in search results (JSON lists of domains or patterns, where *
# is any characters: *.ua is every .ua site):
# TINYLM_SEARCH_INCLUDE_DOMAINS=["ign.com","gamespot.com","*.ua"]
# TINYLM_SEARCH_EXCLUDE_DOMAINS=["pinterest.com"]
# Where models, collections and training runs are stored.
# TINYLM_DATA_DIR=/data/tinylm-studio
# CPU threads for answers (default: physical cores, at most 8) and chunks added per question.
# TINYLM_THREADS=8
# TINYLM_RAG_TOP_K=4
# Require this key from API clients (Authorization: Bearer ... or x-api-key).
# TINYLM_API_KEY=
# PyTorch build installed by `make setup-engine`: cpu (default) or auto (GPU, for training).
# TINYLM_TORCH=cpu
# API keys of teachers for generating training examples (OpenRouter, Anthropic, ...) are not set
# here: add them in the app under Models -> Teachers; they are stored in the workspace database.
# Exporting fine-tuned models to GGUF downloads llama.cpp's converter from PyPI once; offline, use
# a llama.cpp checkout instead.
# TINYLM_LLAMA_CPP_DIR=/path/to/llama.cpp
# Any other engine setting from docs/api.md can go here too.
